      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High-density zoning in big cities is often criticized for leading to overcrowding, which can strain public services and infrastructure. Critics argue that it results in increased traffic congestion, pollution, and a decline in the quality of life. They believe that high-density zoning encourages urban sprawl, which can lead to the loss of green spaces and negatively impact the environment. Additionally, opponents claim that it can drive up housing prices, making it difficult for lower-income residents to afford homes in these areas. They also argue that it can lead to a lack of community cohesion and a decrease in property values for existing homeowners.",
